<body>

    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="muted">
        <strong>Touch Grass Simulator</strong> &middot; published by Maffin<br>
        Last updated: 26 June 2026
    </p>

    <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains what information the mobile game <strong>Touch Grass Simulator</strong>
        (the &ldquo;Game&rdquo;) collects, how it is used, and the choices you have. By installing or playing the
        Game, you agree to this policy. If you do not agree, please do not use the Game.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
    <p>
        You do <strong>not</strong> need to give us your real name or email to play. We and our service providers
        collect the following:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Account identifiers:</strong> when you first play, an <strong>anonymous player ID</strong> is
            created through Unity Gaming Services so your progress can be saved. If you choose to sign in with
            <strong>Google Play Games</strong>, your progress is also linked to your Google Play account.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Profile you choose:</strong> a <strong>display name</strong> and an in-game <strong>avatar</strong>
            (selected from a built-in set &mdash; we do not collect photos). Your display name and avatar are
            <strong>public</strong>: they are shown to other players on leaderboards and inside guilds.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Saved game progress:</strong> your in-game progress (such as score, upgrades, garden, currencies,
            and settings) is stored in the cloud and tied to your player ID so it can sync across sessions and
            devices.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Guild &amp; social content:</strong> if you join or create a guild, we store your guild
            membership, the guild&rsquo;s name, description and banner, your contributions, and any
            <strong>chat messages</strong> you send. Chat messages are visible to other members of your guild and
            pass through an automated profanity filter.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Device &amp; technical data:</strong> device model, operating-system version, language, screen
            settings, and a mobile <strong>advertising identifier</strong> (e.g. Google Advertising ID).
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Network data:</strong> IP address and an approximate (city/country-level) location derived from
            it.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Usage &amp; diagnostics:</strong> in-game events (such as taps, upgrades, and sessions),
            performance data, and crash reports.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Purchase data:</strong> records of in-app purchases and subscriptions (for example
            &ldquo;Remove Ads&rdquo;). Payments are processed by <strong>Google Play</strong>; we do
            <strong>not</strong> receive or store your full payment-card details.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>2. How We Use Information</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>To run, save, and synchronise the Game and your progress.</li>
        <li>To provide online features such as leaderboards, profiles, and guilds (including guild chat).</li>
        <li>To display and measure advertising, including frequency capping and reward delivery.</li>
        <li>To process and validate in-app purchases, subscriptions, and in-game currencies.</li>
        <li>To moderate display names and chat, and to prevent fraud, cheating, and abuse.</li>
        <li>To analyse performance, fix crashes, and improve the Game.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Advertising</h2>
    <p>
        We use <strong>Unity LevelPlay</strong> (ironSource) to show ads, which mediates ads from third-party
        networks. To serve and measure ads, these providers may use your advertising identifier and similar data; how
        they handle it is governed by their own privacy policies, listed in &sect;4 &mdash; we don&rsquo;t restate them
        here. Buying &ldquo;Remove Ads&rdquo; stops ads from being shown.
    </p>
    <p>You can limit ad tracking at any time:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Reset or delete your advertising ID:</strong> Android <em>Settings &rarr; Privacy &rarr; Ads</em>.</li>
        <li>
            Players in the EEA, UK, and other applicable regions are shown a <strong>consent prompt</strong> on first
            launch and can change their choice at any time.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. Third-Party Service Providers</h2>
    <p>We rely on the following providers, each of which processes data under its own privacy policy:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            Unity Technologies (Unity Gaming Services &mdash; Authentication, Cloud Save, Leaderboards,
            Economy, Analytics, and LevelPlay) &mdash;
            <a href="https://unity.com/legal/privacy-policy">unity.com/legal/privacy-policy</a>
        </li>
        <li>
            ironSource / Unity LevelPlay &mdash;
            <a href="https://www.is.com/privacy-policy/">is.com/privacy-policy</a>
        </li>
        <li>
            Google (Google Play services, Google Play Games, AdMob, Google Play Billing) &mdash;
            <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">policies.google.com/privacy</a>
        </li>
        <li>AppLovin &mdash; <a href="https://www.applovin.com/privacy/">applovin.com/privacy</a></li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        The Game also operates our own server to store your saved progress, guilds, and chat. If you choose to join
        our community <strong>Discord</strong> server from within the Game, your use of Discord is governed by
        <a href="https://discord.com/privacy">Discord&rsquo;s privacy policy</a>; we only see aggregate, non-personal
        information such as the current number of online players.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Data Sharing</h2>
    <p>
        We do <strong>not</strong> sell your personal information. We share data only with the service providers
        listed in this policy so they can perform their functions (such as serving ads, saving your progress, and
        processing purchases), with other players where you choose to be social (your public display name, avatar,
        score, and guild chat), and where required by law.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Data Retention &amp; Deletion</h2>
    <p>
        We keep data only as long as needed for the purposes above. You can clear local data by uninstalling the
        Game or resetting progress in its settings. To request deletion of your cloud-saved progress, guild data, and
        chat history associated with your player ID, contact us at the address below and we will delete it within a
        reasonable period, except where we must retain certain records to comply with the law or prevent abuse.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Children&rsquo;s Privacy</h2>
    <p>
        The Game is not directed to children under 13 (or under 16 in the EEA), and we do not knowingly collect
        personal information from them. If you believe a child has provided us data, contact us and we will delete it.
        Please do not share personal information about yourself or others in guild chat.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Your Rights</h2>
    <p>
        Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct, delete, or restrict the processing of
        your personal data, to object to processing, to data portability, and (for California residents) to opt out of
        the &ldquo;sale&rdquo; or &ldquo;sharing&rdquo; of personal information. To exercise these rights, contact us
        using the details below.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Security</h2>
    <p>
        We use reasonable technical and organisational safeguards to protect your data, including encrypted
        connections to our server and to our providers. No method of transmission or storage is 100% secure, however,
        and we cannot guarantee absolute security. Please avoid sharing sensitive personal information in guild chat.
    </p>

    <h2>10. International Transfers</h2>
    <p>
        Your information may be processed on servers located outside your country, including in regions with
        different data-protection laws. Where required, our providers use appropriate safeguards for such transfers.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Material changes will be reflected by updating the
        &ldquo;Last updated&rdquo; date above and, where appropriate, through an in-game notice.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Contact Us</h2>
    <p>
        Questions or requests regarding this policy or your data:<br>
        <strong>Maffin</strong><br>
        Email: <a href="mailto:REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_CONTACT_EMAIL">REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_CONTACT_EMAIL</a>
    </p>

    <p class="note">
        <strong>Before publishing:</strong> replace
        <code>REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_CONTACT_EMAIL</code> above with the support email you want shown publicly (Google Play
        requires a working contact + data-deletion path).
    </p>

</body>
</html>
